WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.265
[ Watch on KissFlix.co ]

2
00:06.535 --> 00:07.535
No, I didn't mean it.

3
00:08.345 --> 00:09.345
I'm sorry.

4
00:09.705 --> 00:10.705
I'm so sorry.

5
00:10.735 --> 00:12.475
I said such awful things.

6
00:13.145 --> 00:14.145
I'm sorry.

7
00:16.525 --> 00:17.525
Forgive me.

8
00:19.285 --> 00:21.515
Miwa, calm down first.

9
00:21.885 --> 00:22.885
Saeko.

10
00:23.455 --> 00:24.825
Saeko, please.

11
00:24.855 --> 00:26.624
Without you, I...

12
00:26.625 --> 00:27.884
Okay, I get it.

13
00:27.885 --> 00:28.885
I get it already.

14
00:29.095 --> 00:32.395
Saeko, without you...

15
00:34.635 --> 00:35.735
Saeko...

16
00:42.335 --> 00:44.875
This is all your fault, Miwa.

17
00:50.675 --> 00:52.515
So I'm going to do whatever I want.

18
00:53.885 --> 00:57.015
From now on, I'll only come to you for this.

19
01:36.205 --> 01:43.705
"How Do We Relationship?"

20
01:48.605 --> 01:50.405
(Final Episode: Smile in the Sunlight)

21
01:50.475 --> 01:51.375
Good work today.

22
01:51.385 --> 01:52.485
Hey there.

23
01:53.875 --> 01:54.545
Hey everyone...

24
01:54.545 --> 01:55.425
- Long time no see. - Hey.

25
01:55.425 --> 01:56.425
Long time no see.

26
01:59.785 --> 02:02.585
Miwa, are you feeling better now?

27
02:03.555 --> 02:06.384
Yeah. Sorry for making you guys worry.

28
02:06.385 --> 02:07.895
Not at all!

29
02:07.925 --> 02:09.254
I'm just glad you're feeling better.

30
02:09.255 --> 02:10.255
Yeah, seriously.

31
02:10.295 --> 02:13.294
You took about a week off.

32
02:13.295 --> 02:14.535
Did you catch the flu?

33
02:20.951 --> 02:22.705
Just a cold that dragged on.

34
02:24.775 --> 02:25.904
Anyway, glad you're okay.

35
02:25.905 --> 02:28.814
All right, shall we get started?

36
02:28.815 --> 02:29.605
Let's do it.

37
02:29.605 --> 02:30.605
Time to practice!

38
02:31.385 --> 02:33.815
How long are you going to cry?

39
02:33.915 --> 02:35.715
It's nothing to cry over.

40
02:37.255 --> 02:40.825
But... I caused trouble for everyone.

41
02:41.025 --> 02:42.725
Nobody thinks that.

42
02:43.025 --> 02:45.095
Just practice more and make up for it.

43
02:47.935 --> 02:50.235
I don't want to be in the club anymore.

44
02:53.405 --> 02:54.905
I see.

45
02:56.605 --> 03:00.175
Then we won't have any reason to cross paths. Are you okay with that?

46
03:00.245 --> 03:01.885
You don't care if you never see me again?

47
03:03.375 --> 03:04.375
I do care.

48
03:05.385 --> 03:07.015
Then aren't you quitting the club?

49
03:07.485 --> 03:09.715
I... won't quit.

50
03:09.985 --> 03:11.655
Then hang in there.

51
03:12.765 --> 03:14.155
Saeko.

52
03:16.425 --> 03:17.865
When we get back,

53
03:18.725 --> 03:19.925
can we do it again?

54
03:22.965 --> 03:23.965
Sure.

55
03:26.065 --> 03:27.035
Saeko.

56
03:27.036 --> 03:28.775
Wait.

57
03:29.035 --> 03:30.035
No kissing.

58
03:30.675 --> 03:32.845
And don't say my name when we're doing this.

59
03:35.275 --> 03:36.515
Why?

60
03:48.625 --> 03:49.955
I'm sorry.

61
03:51.665 --> 03:53.995
For always making you go along with what I want.

62
03:55.295 --> 03:56.495
Even though I...

63
03:57.465 --> 03:59.965
can't give you anything in return.

64
04:05.005 --> 04:06.005
Whatever.

65
04:06.705 --> 04:09.275
I'm just satisfying my own urges anyway.

66
04:18.785 --> 04:19.985
Sae-chan.

67
04:20.885 --> 04:22.025
Yeah?

68
04:23.395 --> 04:24.965
What's with that look on your face?

69
04:25.065 --> 04:26.065
Huh?

70
04:26.865 --> 04:29.295
You had the weirdest look on your face just now.

71
04:29.535 --> 04:30.765
Oh...

72
04:31.405 --> 04:34.335
I just don't know what I'm doing anymore.

73
04:34.575 --> 04:37.975
Feels like right and wrong don't even matter now.

74
04:43.215 --> 04:44.415
Are you okay?

75
04:47.085 --> 04:48.755
Who knows...

76
04:50.085 --> 04:51.925
Sounds rough.

77
05:18.085 --> 05:20.445
I should probably start packing up my stuff.

78
05:32.225 --> 05:33.765
Are we...

79
05:35.395 --> 05:37.835
considered dating right now?

80
05:44.105 --> 05:46.105
I don't think I can finish this.

81
05:46.175 --> 05:47.545
I'm so full.

82
05:49.275 --> 05:51.515
Give it to me, then.

83
05:57.855 --> 05:59.785
You sure have a big appetite.

84
06:12.005 --> 06:13.335
Hey, Saeko.

85
06:13.665 --> 06:14.665
Hmm?

86
06:15.635 --> 06:17.235
Hold me when we get back, okay?

87
06:19.805 --> 06:21.415
Where did that come from?

88
06:21.475 --> 06:23.355
Don't say stuff like that in a place like this.

89
06:23.445 --> 06:24.515
Why not?

90
06:24.885 --> 06:26.015
What does it matter?

91
06:35.995 --> 06:38.195
Miwa, are you really okay with this?

92
06:40.265 --> 06:42.335
Being friends with benefits with me.

93
06:45.505 --> 06:48.474
We're not... friends with benefits.

94
06:48.475 --> 06:49.135
We're not.

95
06:49.136 --> 06:50.905
We're textbook friends with benefits.

96
07:03.715 --> 07:05.555
Do you want to go back to being friends?

97
07:12.695 --> 07:13.795
We're...

98
07:16.535 --> 07:19.565
way past the point of going back to being just friends.

99
07:34.085 --> 07:35.585
Saeko...

100
07:36.155 --> 07:37.555
I'm sorry.

101
07:39.385 --> 07:40.485
What's wrong?

102
07:40.825 --> 07:42.125
Post-climax clarity?

103
07:44.155 --> 07:47.125
Why am I so awful?

104
07:48.595 --> 07:50.595
I'm always so selfish,

105
07:51.335 --> 07:53.435
only thinking about myself.

106
07:56.205 --> 07:57.805
I want to change,

107
07:58.475 --> 07:59.905
but I just can't seem to do it.

108
08:03.215 --> 08:04.915
I want to die.

109
08:11.825 --> 08:13.255
Listen,

110
08:13.525 --> 08:15.395
can you stop throwing that phrase around?

111
08:16.325 --> 08:18.465
Because I really do.

112
08:18.995 --> 08:20.425
Yeah, right.

113
08:20.895 --> 08:23.595
Would someone who actually wants to die eat two bowls of ramen

114
08:24.065 --> 08:25.765
and climax twice during sex?

115
08:26.435 --> 08:28.405
It wasn't two bowls, it was one and a half!

116
08:28.505 --> 08:30.305
That's the part you're arguing with?

117
08:36.475 --> 08:38.985
You just think I'm saying it for attention anyway.

118
08:42.415 --> 08:45.255
Just stop saying you want to die.

119
08:46.425 --> 08:48.125
Even though I say it a lot too.

120
08:49.795 --> 08:50.904
Because it's convenient, right?

121
08:50.905 --> 08:51.905
Saying you want to die...

122
08:52.165 --> 08:54.565
lets you stop thinking and play the tragic heroine.

123
08:57.065 --> 08:58.205
That's so mean...

124
09:00.765 --> 09:02.935
If you're going to turn your brain off anyway,

125
09:03.675 --> 09:05.175
you're better off sleeping, eating,

126
09:05.805 --> 09:07.375
or having dirty thoughts.

127
09:07.975 --> 09:11.015
Using your head for that stuff is way more productive.

128
09:21.295 --> 09:22.625
Saeko.

129
09:23.925 --> 09:25.395
Let's do it one more time.

130
09:26.425 --> 09:28.095
Didn't we just finish?

131
09:30.435 --> 09:33.465
As long as my head is filled with things that feel good,

132
09:34.005 --> 09:35.635
I feel like I can forget

133
09:37.305 --> 09:39.645
everything about getting dumped.

134
09:42.545 --> 09:44.215
So you did get dumped.

135
09:47.885 --> 09:49.055
Is that bad?

136
09:49.355 --> 09:50.355
Not really.

137
09:51.485 --> 09:53.955
Just sucks for you, I guess.

138
09:59.625 --> 10:00.825
Um...

139
10:02.495 --> 10:03.965
Saeko.

140
10:05.165 --> 10:07.135
I'm sorry about so many things.

141
10:07.705 --> 10:09.335
It's no big deal, don't sweat it.

142
10:10.875 --> 10:12.775
Even though you're not even my girlfriend.

143
10:13.445 --> 10:14.445
I'm sorry.

144
10:31.265 --> 10:32.195
Catch!

145
10:32.265 --> 10:33.365
Oh, nice pitch!

146
10:33.925 --> 10:35.895
Wait, why are we playing catch?

147
10:36.195 --> 10:37.195
Hmm?

148
10:37.465 --> 10:40.935
I figured it might help take your mind off things.

149
10:40.985 --> 10:41.985
Nice ball!

150
10:44.075 --> 10:45.305
You know,

151
10:46.305 --> 10:48.875
I really like you, Yuria.

152
10:54.315 --> 10:55.864
Wh-What's wrong?

153
10:55.865 --> 10:57.085
Did I say something weird?

154
10:59.055 --> 11:00.055
Oh, no.

155
11:01.295 --> 11:05.865
It just reminded me that my ex used to say she liked me a lot, too.

156
11:06.895 --> 11:08.295
Hey, hold on.

157
11:10.265 --> 11:12.835
Don't lump me in with that woman.

158
11:13.305 --> 11:15.305
I don't just say that to anyone, you know.

159
11:15.385 --> 11:16.385
Oh...

160
11:18.045 --> 11:19.675
I only say it to you.

161
11:27.145 --> 11:28.785
Really?

162
11:29.455 --> 11:30.615
Yeah.

163
11:32.185 --> 11:33.285
Come to think of it,

164
11:35.395 --> 11:39.125
I don't think I ever properly told my ex that I liked her.

165
11:43.135 --> 11:44.605
Sae-chan?

166
11:44.765 --> 11:45.965
Oh.

167
11:46.235 --> 11:47.975
I really want some ice cream.

168
11:55.675 --> 11:57.115
Are you okay?

169
12:00.515 --> 12:01.585
I just feel like,

170
12:02.315 --> 12:03.885
looking back on it now,

171
12:04.925 --> 12:07.855
I never really gave her anything.

172
12:09.925 --> 12:12.165
I just ignored my own faults,

173
12:12.795 --> 12:14.635
and because I couldn't get what I wanted,

174
12:14.965 --> 12:17.365
I'd sulk and lash out.

175
12:20.105 --> 12:21.875
I was the worst.

176
12:22.435 --> 12:24.205
It's fine.

177
12:24.235 --> 12:26.505
My ex-girlfriend was way worse.

178
12:26.675 --> 12:28.375
You're nothing compared to her, Sae-chan.

179
12:28.415 --> 12:29.915
What kind of pep talk is that?

180
12:32.915 --> 12:36.115
You're not the worst, Sae-chan.

181
12:37.285 --> 12:38.285
No...

182
12:39.785 --> 12:42.125
I'm still the worst right now.

183
12:44.465 --> 12:45.465
But...

184
12:47.165 --> 12:49.965
I liked her so much that it made me act that way.

185
12:50.265 --> 12:51.265
That much,

186
12:53.205 --> 12:54.605
I finally understand now.

187
13:11.885 --> 13:12.925
Thank you,

188
13:13.425 --> 13:14.425
Yuria.

189
13:25.335 --> 13:26.605
Hey, Miwa.

190
13:26.765 --> 13:27.765
Hmm?

191
13:28.675 --> 13:30.475
I'm not doing it today.

192
13:33.605 --> 13:34.615
Why?

193
13:35.475 --> 13:37.985
No reason in particular.

194
13:40.385 --> 13:42.415
I want to go back to being normal friends.

195
13:44.525 --> 13:45.555
Is that not okay?

196
13:46.285 --> 13:47.285
No, it's not.

197
13:48.025 --> 13:49.495
Why not?

198
13:50.595 --> 13:52.665
You don't even like me that way, Miwa.

199
13:54.735 --> 13:56.095
That's not true...

200
13:57.135 --> 13:58.465
To me, Saeko,

201
13:59.265 --> 14:00.605
you're someone really special.

202
14:03.835 --> 14:05.175
Thank you.

203
14:15.315 --> 14:19.355
Oh, come on. Don't cry!

204
14:19.565 --> 14:22.495
It's just, Saeko, you...

205
14:24.295 --> 14:25.695
All right, fine.

206
14:25.865 --> 14:27.395
I'll stay with you for today.

207
14:28.595 --> 14:29.735
Really?

208
14:30.135 --> 14:31.135
Yeah.

209
14:32.235 --> 14:34.265
I'll do whatever you want today.

210
14:38.775 --> 14:39.775
However,

211
14:40.175 --> 14:43.215
today is the absolute last time we're doing this.

212
14:49.755 --> 14:51.555
Being this close to you feels so warm.

213
14:54.495 --> 14:55.495
Yeah.

214
15:01.765 --> 15:02.765
Hold on.

215
15:03.765 --> 15:04.965
No kissing.

216
15:07.165 --> 15:09.105
What's the big deal with just one kiss?

217
15:09.535 --> 15:12.245
Didn't you say you'd do whatever I wanted today?

218
15:12.375 --> 15:13.375
I'm sorry.

219
15:14.305 --> 15:16.215
Please, anything but kissing.

220
15:17.375 --> 15:19.185
I'm willing to do anything else.

221
15:20.545 --> 15:22.085
You can do whatever you want to me.

222
15:35.735 --> 15:36.735
Miwa.

223
15:37.265 --> 15:38.565
I'm heading home.

224
15:42.605 --> 15:44.405
Out like a light.

225
15:45.345 --> 15:47.375
You could at least see me off for our last time.

226
15:56.485 --> 15:58.985
I really did have feelings for you, Miwa.

227
16:03.355 --> 16:04.995
I was so in love with you.

228
16:29.655 --> 16:34.185
Sociolinguistics isn't sociology; ultimately, it's a branch of linguistics.

229
16:34.595 --> 16:38.795
Though the two are easily confused, the focus of their research is completely different.

230
17:03.985 --> 17:05.885
Oh, hey, Miwa. Good job today.

231
17:19.635 --> 17:21.835
What are we playing for the welcome gig?

232
17:22.785 --> 17:25.645
Hmm, what should we do?

233
17:26.005 --> 17:28.815
Oh, how about Sakanaction or something?

234
17:29.715 --> 17:30.715
Saeko!

235
17:31.885 --> 17:32.645
Hmm?

236
17:32.645 --> 17:33.645
Um...

237
17:34.605 --> 17:35.605
Today too...

238
17:35.955 --> 17:37.435
Do you want to come over to my place?

239
17:40.555 --> 17:41.955
Sure, I guess.

240
17:43.695 --> 17:44.795
Wait a second!

241
17:45.495 --> 17:46.735
We're done with that, remember?

242
17:48.565 --> 17:50.535
Didn't we agree to go back to being friends?

243
17:51.165 --> 17:54.535
But do we really have to go back to just being friends?

244
17:56.405 --> 17:59.845
Because you said you loved me, Saeko.

245
18:05.885 --> 18:06.885
I'm sorry.

246
18:08.455 --> 18:10.315
I accidentally overheard you yesterday.

247
18:11.555 --> 18:14.525
Ugh, that's the worst. I can't believe you heard that...

248
18:14.825 --> 18:15.994
Hey, Saeko!

249
18:15.995 --> 18:17.054
Come on, let's go home together!

250
18:17.055 --> 18:18.324
Please, Saeko!

251
18:18.325 --> 18:19.365
Stop it.

252
18:20.095 --> 18:21.795
Why are you still hanging on to this now?

253
18:22.235 --> 18:24.635
You never even really looked at me.

254
18:25.905 --> 18:27.264
I did try to understand you!

255
18:27.265 --> 18:30.204
I've always wanted to know more about you!

256
18:30.205 --> 18:33.705
Like your past, and what's going through your head right now.

257
18:33.875 --> 18:36.045
I've always wanted to know!

258
18:37.815 --> 18:40.315
You were the one who refused to open up to me, Saeko!

259
19:19.085 --> 19:20.085
Wait!

260
19:20.255 --> 19:21.755
Wait for me, Saeko!

261
19:22.995 --> 19:24.195
Saeko!

262
19:24.895 --> 19:25.895
Hold on!

263
19:27.195 --> 19:28.195
Saeko!

264
19:28.295 --> 19:32.065
All this time, I thought you were the one who didn't have feelings for me!

265
19:37.435 --> 19:38.605
When we started dating,

266
19:39.705 --> 19:40.875
and when we broke up...

267
19:41.815 --> 19:42.815
How do I put it...

268
19:44.075 --> 19:46.035
You were so nonchalant about it all, weren't you?

269
19:48.155 --> 19:49.215
So I figured...

270
19:50.185 --> 19:52.185
the reason we ended up like this

271
19:53.555 --> 19:54.925
was just a whim for you,

272
19:56.225 --> 19:59.895
or simply out of pity for me...

273
20:07.365 --> 20:08.435
It's true.

274
20:11.075 --> 20:13.175
At first, it really was just a whim.

275
20:14.845 --> 20:16.945
I figured we could give dating a shot,

276
20:17.375 --> 20:19.145
or that I just wanted to sleep with you.

277
20:20.015 --> 20:21.355
It wasn't any deeper than that.

278
20:23.255 --> 20:24.655
Then when did it happen?

279
20:26.755 --> 20:28.395
When did you fall for me?

280
20:29.555 --> 20:30.925
How should I know?

281
20:35.895 --> 20:37.465
I don't even know myself.

282
20:41.675 --> 20:42.975
Before I knew it,

283
20:45.105 --> 20:47.675
I had already fallen for you.

284
20:52.385 --> 20:54.785
Isn't that how falling in love works?

285
21:01.825 --> 21:02.825
Yeah...

286
21:05.265 --> 21:06.265
I know.

287
21:09.295 --> 21:10.335
That's why...

288
21:12.765 --> 21:15.805
that's how I want someone to fall in love with me, too.

289
21:17.875 --> 21:19.005
Trying desperately,

290
21:19.575 --> 21:20.905
and bending over backward

291
21:22.845 --> 21:25.745
to force yourself to love someone is just wrong.

292
21:36.025 --> 21:37.425
You know that too, right?

293
21:41.635 --> 21:42.735
Which means...

294
21:45.565 --> 21:47.735
this can never work between us.

295
22:04.725 --> 22:06.655
I don't want to understand that at all!

296
23:01.915 --> 23:03.814
We're the Light Music Club! Check us out!

297
23:03.815 --> 23:05.014
We're from the Light Music Club.

298
23:05.015 --> 23:06.215
Here's a flyer for you!

299
23:06.885 --> 23:08.484
How was your first date?

300
23:08.485 --> 23:10.015
Did you guys kiss?

301
23:10.505 --> 23:11.924
We only just started dating.

302
23:11.925 --> 23:13.365
There's no way we'd kiss right away.

303
23:13.605 --> 23:16.625
Huh? You kissed me right off the bat when we started dating.

304
23:16.695 --> 23:18.925
We're the Light Music Club! Check us out!

305
23:19.325 --> 23:21.165
We're from the Light Music Club.

306
23:25.865 --> 23:27.165
Oh, are you okay?

307
23:28.135 --> 23:30.235
By the way, any interest in the Light Music Club?

308
23:30.275 --> 23:31.275
Hey, come on...

309
23:31.276 --> 23:32.904
What's the harm in asking, right?

310
23:32.905 --> 23:34.615
At least take a flyer, please?

311
23:44.111 --> 23:47.645
University Sophmore, Spring.
